{"id": "EUVD-2026-95126", "enisaUuid": "4f0e8fd7-b79a-387f-a415-c91ac314d63a", "description": "FFmpeg before 7.1.4 and 8.0.x before 8.0.2 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability in ff_rtsp_connect() in libavformat/rtsp.c that follows RTSP 3xx redirects without validating the Location URL. Malicious RTSP servers can redirect FFmpeg to internal hosts and ports under other schemes, bypassing -protocol_whitelist, to probe internal network services.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T17:30:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T17:51:31", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/ea9e85e54981b8402368d0f21648836d6738f1b1", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/2326bc5f69c9", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/7c011995e394", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/f9aa8729bce1", "https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/22292", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n7.1.3/libavformat/rtsp.c#L2016", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-before-7.1.4-and-8.0.2-ssrf-via-rtsp-redirect-handling"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jhxg-38qw-fjxv", "CVE-2026-107698"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05b35b30-52ee-332f-a215-bf7ac7816ac7", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "8.0 <8.0.2"}, {"id": "6b7c3137-7919-3973-9774-26d09ea47254", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "0 <7.1.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0e5915a0-e639-3fe5-a3f4-d35ede89d8c3", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}], "isExploited": false}